n, A. Nishi, N. N. Starkova, A. A. Fienberg, A. C. Nairn, D. J. Surmeier, and P. Greengard. <year>2004</year>. A network of control mediated by regulator of calcium/calmodulin-dependent signaling. <source>Science.</source> <volume>306</volume>:<fpage>698</fpage>&#x02013;701.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15499021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hudmon, A., and H. Schulman. <year>2002</year>. Neuronal CA<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase II: the role of structure and autoregulation in cellular function. <source>Annu. Rev. Biochem.</source> <volume>71</volume>:<fpage>473</fpage>&#x02013;510.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12045104</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Meyer, T., P. I. Hanson, L. Stryer, and H. Schulman. <year>1992</year>. Calmodulin trapping by calcium-calmodulin-dependent protein kinase. <source>Science.</source> <volume>256</volume>:<fpage>1199</fpage>&#x02013;1202.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1317063</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Putkey, J. A., and M. N. Waxham. <year>1996</year>. A peptide model for calmodulin trapping by calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase II. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>271</volume>:<fpage>29619</fpage>&#x02013;29623.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8939892</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Colbran, R. J. <year>2004</year>. Protein phosphatases and calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase II-dependent synaptic plasticity. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>8404</fpage>&#x02013;8409.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15456812</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Lisman, J., H. Schulman, and H. Cline. <year>2002</year>. The molecular basis of CaMKII function in synaptic and behavioural memory. <source>Nat. Rev. Neurosci.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>175</fpage>&#x02013;190.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11994750</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Berridge, M. J., M. D. Bootman, and H. L. Roderick. <year>2003</year>. Calcium signalling: dynamics, homeostasis and remodelling. <source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>4</volume>:<fpage>517</fpage>&#x02013;529.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12838335</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Pitt, G. S. <year>2007</year>. Calmodulin and CaMKII as molecular switches for cardiac ion channels. <source>Cardiovasc. Res.</source> <volume>73</volume>:<fpage>641</fpage>&#x02013;647.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17137569</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Schulman, H., P. I. Hanson, and T. Meyer. <year>1992</year>. Decoding calcium signals by multifunctional CaM kinase. <source>Cell Calcium.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>401</fpage>&#x02013;411.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1324121</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Black, D. J., Q. K. Tran, and A. Persechini. <year>2004</year>. Monitoring the total available calmodulin concentration in intact cells over the physiological range in free Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>. <source>Cell Calcium.</source> <volume>35</volume>:<fpage>415</fpage>&#x02013;425.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15003851</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gough, A. H., and D. L. Taylor. <year>1993</year>. Fluorescence anisotropy imaging microscopy maps calmodulin binding during cellular contraction and locomotion. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>121</volume>:<fpage>1095</fpage>&#x02013;1107.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8501117</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Tran, Q. K.,